  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2010-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "First, we get \\[2^{24} = (2^8)(4^8) < (2^8)(5^8) = 10^8.\\]\n\nNext, we get \\[10^8 = (2^8)(5^8) = \\]\\[(4^4)(5^8) < (5^4)(5^8) = 5^{12}.\\] This means \\(2^{24} < 10^8 < 5^{12} .\\)\n\nThus, the answer is A .",
      "hints": [
        "Compare \\(2^{24}\\), \\(10^8=(2\\cdot5)^8\\), and \\(5^{12}\\).",
        "Rewrite the powers so they have comparable eighth-power factors."
      ],
